From c13af57a70cf96083ed43939a98e34c04d7a498c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noel Blatter <noel.blatter@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:13:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Signal entries go straight into the value store of the signal
 matrices

The forward pass evaluated the signal entries into an array of their own
(1893 entries x 101 frequencies, 3 MB) only to copy them into the value store
of the signal matrices right afterwards. When every written entry has a row
of its own in the store, which is the usual case, the entry block now writes
into those rows directly (_EntryBlock.run(store=...)). The store is created
and filled with the constant entries beforehand (SystemPlan.signal_store).
forward() receives a _StoredEntries in place of the array; if the store is
needed a second time (the native factorization asks for the values again
after an unstable pivot sequence), it is rebuilt from the entries. Callers
that pass an array of entries work as before.

Page faults of the first forward call on x86-64 with the native kernel:
4028 -> 3562. The times are at the limit of what can be measured here:
emulated x86-64, 8 alternating runs, forward phase 50.6 -> 49.9 ms and warm
run 21.9 -> 21.2 ms; no difference on arm64. Outputs bit-identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
